WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.120
I'm the dark,

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.420
knuckle-dragging,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.880
right-wing,

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.689
Republican former governor of the

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.789
state of Texas.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.949
Former Republican, Texas governor

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.719
and Trump administration Energy

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.849
Secretary Rick Perry was

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.829
the most surprising speaker at

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.899
the 2023 Psychedelics

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.849
Science Conference held in Denver

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.749
this June.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.309
Some of you are out there going,

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.199
"What in the hell

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.149
is that dude doing

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.150
on this stage?"

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:33.929
Organized by the Multidisciplinary

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.999
Association for Psychedelic Studies,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.529
a group that has been pushing for

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.659
FDA approval of MDMA

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.279
assisted therapy since the late

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.199
1980s, the conference was

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.809
attended by a reported 13,000

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.189
people.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.019
Perry sat down with Reason to

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.209
explain why he believes psychedelics

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.709
should be legal medicine for

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.569
veterans and others suffering from

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.429
PTSD, how to allow

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.469
more immigrants to come to America

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.779
lawfully and why, if

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.759
he were ever to take a psychedelic

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.979
drug, it would be ibogaine,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.809
a notoriously powerful

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.849
substance made from the bark

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.050
of an African tree.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.699
Rick Perry, thanks for talking to

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.989
Reason.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:18.508
You as well Nick.

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:20.629
You were speaking at a psychedelic

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:21.889
conference.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.299
What is so important about

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.249
psychedelics that have brought

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.229
you, a conservative Republican,

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.089
to speak to people who

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.949
as you said in your opening remarks,

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.449
probably were wondering why you were

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:32.749
there?

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.959
Yeah, When I got introduced to this,

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.879
approximately five years ago,

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.859
it was through a young man

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.779
who worked with me at the Department

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.819
of Energy. At that point in my life,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.189
I was the secretary of energy, and

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.999
he was seeing

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.679
some of his colleagues in the

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.789
special operations world.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.260
This was a former Navy SEAL

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.559
who, interestingly today is a

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.389
United States congressman who

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.819
is very vocal, very supportive

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.279
of the use of psychedelics for

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:05.869
post-traumatic stress.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.729
And he's

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.709
the one that started

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.780
working with me on this.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.989
Me getting comfortable that

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:17.299
Rick Perry and psychedelics

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.279
in the same sentence was

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.199
even even close

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.909
to a reality.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.829
And his

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.049
twin brother, Marcus Luttrell,

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.729
who was the author of "Lone

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.319
Survivor," the book and then the

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.329
movie was made about his

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.619
experiences.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.509
That brother lived

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.859
with us at the governor's mansion

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.809
for two-plus years as

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.639
we were, my wife

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.099
and I were learning about

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.929
post-traumatic stress and how

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.399
poor our government was in dealing

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.329
with this, frankly.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.069
And we were trying to find solutions

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.289
to help heal this young man.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.329
And so all of that

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.129
collectively through the years

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.679
brought me to a comfort level

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.819
that.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.619
I'm a results oriented guy.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:01.759
You know, the process is the

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.139
process. I get it.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.539
But what's the result?

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.549
And what I've seen over the last

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.589
four years in particular,

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.779
studying this, talking

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.310
to myriad of

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.369
young men in this case,

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:17.779
there have been young women that

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.989
have gone to Mexico as well.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.479
I've just not had conversations with

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.529
any of those.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:23.359
But these young men who have

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.159
put their lives on the line for us,

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.630
who have been impacted

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.689
through all the different types of

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:31.489
trauma that come with being a war

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.080
fighter, that

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.989
this treatment,

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.969
this medicine works.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.139
And so

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.229
I've also, you know,

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.999
educated myself about the history of

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.009
this and why psychedelics got taken

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.839
away from the research

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.849
world, from the

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.349
citizens at large, from the

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.299
standpoint of being a a medicine

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.199
that could could work.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.089
So it started to make

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.919
a lot of sense to me that,

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.589
you know, these are medicines

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.479
that were taken away for

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.459
political purposes back in the early

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.679
seventies and

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.989
that we need to

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.909
reintegrate, studying

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.859
them, do the appropriate things.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.689
But the potential here

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.789
is stunningly

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:17.569
positive.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.069
I mean, when you just look and I'll

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.989
give you one peek

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.879
at Dr.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:23.959
Rachel Yehuda,

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:27.139
Ph.D., who's working at

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.239
the VA

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.649
in New York.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.149
I think she has two

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:36.980
studies behind them,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Phase three

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.229
that are showing just amazing

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.230
results.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.449
Treatment with MDMA, two weeks,

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.450
treatment with MDMA. So

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.119
three treatments in a month period

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.120
of time.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.019
They have classic symptoms,

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.679
anxiety, depression,

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.569
sleeplessness, suicidal thoughts,

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:03.570
one or all of those.

